{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01NrHEtYvTmztQKRJrLhgQSd", "type": "tool_result", "content": "Web search results for query: \"example.com domain IANA\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"m.example.com - robtex.com\",\"url\":\"https://robtex.com/en/dns-lookup/com/example/m\"},{\"title\":\"www.wikipedia.org\",\"url\":\"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Example.com\"},{\"title\":\"vm535076.example.com - robtex.com\",\"url\":\"https://robtex.com/en/dns-lookup/com/example/vm535076\"},{\"title\":\"The domains example.com, example.net, and\",\"url\":\"https://kottke.org/02/03/the-domains-examplecom-examplenet-and\"},{\"title\":\"www.chise.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.chise.org/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Example.com\"},{\"title\":\"graphsearch.epfl.ch\",\"url\":\"https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/concept/1191806\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring The Examplecom Domain Purpose Usage: Why This Famous Website Exists And How To Use It Correctly\",\"url\":\"https://relay2.core.com.tr/famous-website-exists-use-it-l6l3.html\"},{\"title\":\"example.com - dns.ninja\",\"url\":\"https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example\"},{\"title\":\"www.example.com - dns.ninja\",\"url\":\"https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example/www\"},{\"title\":\"physicsforums.com\",\"url\":\"https://physicsforums.com/tags/example-50/wiki\"}]\n\nThe search results consistently say example.com is a reserved domain that IANA holds for documentation, though the sources vary in quality.\n\n- **Reservation and purpose:** Wikipedia describes example.com as one of four second-level names that IANA reserves at the IETF's direction for documentation. Writers can use the names in technical and software documentation, manuals, and sample software configurations.\n- **Origin:** The IETF set the policy in RFC 2606 in 1999. The label has been reserved and registered since at least 1992, and the IETF established the authority of this use in RFC 2606 in 1999.\n- **Use without permission:** The domains may be used in documentation without prior consultation with IANA or ICANN.\n- **Live operation:** In practice, the names are also installed in DNS with IPv4 and IPv6 addresses of a web server managed by ICANN. They are DNSSEC-signed.\n\nSource quality varies. The Wikipedia mirrors and the EPFL page track closely, while robtex and dns.ninja are lookup sites that restate the same facts. One dns.ninja page lists nameservers that changed from IANA's own servers to Cloudflare's in 2026, so the DNS records may have shifted recently. A Turkish hosting-site article is unreliable and I'd disregard its claims.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d26862b9-9cb1-4f7a-bd57-2fd5838e0056", "uuid": "97bf8f2f-0500-4403-a42f-a462b7d01b91", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T09:42:09.551Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "example.com domain IANA", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01HL1UK5xrdmPLjMGkyUMy32", "content": [{"title": "m.example.com - robtex.com", "url": "https://robtex.com/en/dns-lookup/com/example/m"}, {"title": "www.wikipedia.org", "url": "https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Example.com"}, {"title": "vm535076.example.com - robtex.com", "url": "https://robtex.com/en/dns-lookup/com/example/vm535076"}, {"title": "The domains example.com, example.net, and", "url": "https://kottke.org/02/03/the-domains-examplecom-examplenet-and"}, {"title": "www.chise.org", "url": "https://www.chise.org/ipns/en.wikipedia-on-ipfs.org/wiki/Example.com"}, {"title": "graphsearch.epfl.ch", "url": "https://graphsearch.epfl.ch/concept/1191806"}, {"title": "Exploring The Examplecom Domain Purpose Usage: Why This Famous Website Exists And How To Use It Correctly", "url": "https://relay2.core.com.tr/famous-website-exists-use-it-l6l3.html"}, {"title": "example.com - dns.ninja", "url": "https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example"}, {"title": "www.example.com - dns.ninja", "url": "https://dns.ninja/en/dns-lookup/com/example/www"}, {"title": "physicsforums.com", "url": "https://physicsforums.com/tags/example-50/wiki"}]}, "The search results consistently say example.com is a reserved domain that IANA holds for documentation, though the sources vary in quality.\n\n- **Reservation and purpose:** Wikipedia describes example.com as one of four second-level names that IANA reserves at the IETF's direction for documentation. Writers can use the names in technical and software documentation, manuals, and sample software configurations.\n- **Origin:** The IETF set the policy in RFC 2606 in 1999. The label has been reserved and registered since at least 1992, and the IETF established the authority of this use in RFC 2606 in 1999.\n- **Use without permission:** The domains may be used in documentation without prior consultation with IANA or ICANN.\n- **Live operation:** In practice, the names are also installed in DNS with IPv4 and IPv6 addresses of a web server managed by ICANN. They are DNSSEC-signed.\n\nSource quality varies. The Wikipedia mirrors and the EPFL page track closely, while robtex and dns.ninja are lookup sites that restate the same facts. One dns.ninja page lists nameservers that changed from IANA's own servers to Cloudflare's in 2026, so the DNS records may have shifted recently. A Turkish hosting-site article is unreliable and I'd disregard its claims."], "durationSeconds": 5.5880585, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01NrHEtYvTmztQKRJrLhgQSd", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "user_temporary"}}]}
